Functions returning a pointer that GCC 2.8.1 calls where they are not declared, declared before their callers.
Called undeclared, C takes what such a function returns for an int: on a host whose pointers are wider than int
(LP64: 64-bit Linux and macOS) the pointer is cut to 32 bits, and cc1 crashes or compiles wrongly.

--- a/c-decl.c
+++ b/c-decl.c
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@
    line numbers.  For example, the CONST_DECLs for enum values.  */
 
 #include "config.h"
+
+/* Called before they are declared: declared here, so that a host whose pointers are wider than int
+   (LP64) does not take what they return for an int.  */
+extern struct rtx_def *label_rtx ();
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include "tree.h"
 #include "flags.h"
